  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Thylacoleo carnifex, the marsupial lion, in a neutral whole-body stance based on composite fossil anatomy. Soft tissues, coat, ears, colour and size are interpretive; the missing hind-foot hallux tip is conservatively completed. Climbing and tail-bracing remain functional hypotheses, not observed behaviour or a depicted hunting event.",
    "zh": "袋狮 Thylacoleo carnifex 综合化石解剖作中性站姿全身复原。软组织、毛被、耳、颜色及尺寸为解释性补配；缺失的后足拇趾末端作保守补全。攀爬与尾支撑仍属功能推断，不代表已观察行为或特定捕猎事件。"
  },
